  realmDialogue:
  - "Ah... I see. If that is your final decision-cough-I suppose I can\u2019t do anything to change your mind."
  - "R-cough-really, my lord? If that\u2019s your decision, I am be forever grateful. "
  thingsPersonSays:
  - key: Hello... cough, cough... my son, he told you of my condition?
    value:
    - He did. But tell me more.
    - "Ma\u2019am... I can\u2019t let you go into the Human Realm."
  - key: "You\u2019re a compassionate man, my lord... cough... Well... where do I begin..."
    value:
    - ...
    - 
  - key: "Oh... wheezing sounds... well... I suppose there\u2019s not much else to talk about, then..."
    value:
    - ...
    - 
  - key: "Long ago, I was a queen. I birthed a son, who you\u2019ve met, who I loved and doted upon with all my heart."
    value:
    - Where were you the queen of?
    - How did he become so powerful?
  - key: None1
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: But maybe you should consider a little longer... my son... is very powerful, you know.
    value:
    - Are you threatening a Bodhisattva?
    - 
  - key: None2
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "Oh-cough-Kushinakoku. You may know it as the Kingdom of Kushinagar. It\u2019s a beautiful country, my lord."
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "Well, when my husband, when he learned that it\u2019d grant us the most karmic merit possible, sent my boy away into monasticism."
    value:
    - But he is no ordinary monk.
    - 
  - key: "No, my lord, I would never... but his actions are out of my control... and it\u2019s hard to think of a person who wouldn\u2019t be upset were their mother damned to Hell."
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "No, he isn\u2019t. I reckon he became this powerful because of the prayers I poured into him during his studies. It was hard to be away from him for so long. But-cough-I found many ways to support him. I sent him food, clothes, supplies. I spent not a cent on myself."
    value:
    - ...or the temples.
    - How kind of you.
  - key: None4
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "Y-yes... cough... that\u2019s why you see my in the form I\u2019m in today..."
    value:
    - What form is that?
    - 
  - key: Yes, well... perhaps I should have done things differently.
    value:
    - ...
    - ...
  - key: "He described it as becoming a gaki-a hungry ghost. I\u2019m cursed with eternal hunger... and any food I try to eat bursts into flames before it hits my tongue. It\u2019s-cough-excruciating."
    value:
    - Who described it as that?
    - 
  - key: None5
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "My son... he never got the chance to see me before I died. It\u2019s-cough-humiliating... I never wanted him to see me like this..."
    value:
    - ...
    - ...
  - key: None6
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "Oh, my apologies... your mentor did. He\u2019s the one who made me this after all. He said it was a punishment fitting my scrupulousness in life."
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "I\u2019m sorry if... I treated you harshly, Bodhisattva Jizo. I\u2019m just... filled with regret over how I lived my life."
    value:
    - "Do you think you\u2019ve earned a second chance?"
    - "I still can\u2019t send you to the Human Realm."
  - key: None7
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "I like to think so... but of course-cough-that decision isn\u2019t up to me."
    value:
    - 
    - 
  - key: "That\u2019s... okay. I won\u2019t ask you to do that anymore. I\u2019ve made my mistakes."
    value:
    - 
    - 
  endingDialogue:
  - "My lord... you\u2019ve heard everything I have to say. You know of my misdeeds. If you believe I am-cough-still deserving of damnation, do what you must. I apologize, Bodhisattva, if my son gives you trouble for your decision. I have... cough... come to accept that your judgment is fair and just."
  - If you believe I am-cough-still deserving of damnation, do what you must.
